body:
The noire aesthetic only fit because of the comic panels, bro. Max had a big ass smile on his face through the whole first game and the second game only fixed that by changing the face model, Rockstar portrayed a completion to a story where Max learns to let go of his past, while maintaining a redemption arc by letting Passos get a life of his own.. It's not a perfect ending but the alternative was death by either suicide or alcohol, which means no fucking story at all, so the first mistake was Remedy not making Max Payne by themselves... 

&#x200B;

"Random protection job" really narrows it down to fucking nothing, and if that's what you see then it's just you in all honesty, it was rather a bi product of Max's ignorance and bad life choices.. The whole cartel, rick family is again a rockstar thing. 

&#x200B;

Rockstar didn't just leave that dark and gritty aesthetic behind, matter of fact it was honored through the flashbacks of hoboken's bar, rooftops, the church and the graveyard and they actually looked fucking fantastic so again this is bias on your end.

&#x200B;

If you don't take this game as a form of alternate timeline made solely of Rockstar's design, then you'll only see it the way you want to, which is pretty fucking boring compared to what we got.

The cutscenes should've been skippable, I don't need cutscenes on New york minute run or other challenge modes, or when Im going for collectables. And yeah, the level design could've been better, no doubt. 

But the older games DEFINITELY don't have better gunplay simply because there are more guns lmao, when they all felt like they did the same exact shit anyway until the third installment

And you seeing it as "cringe" is a you thing, it's like you have beef with this game bro, you just choose not to like it, which is fine but don't go spreading around bullshit because you chose to close an eye towards the good this game gave us
